136
00:13:55,920 --> 00:14:01,920
From a scientific perspective, the evolution of caffeine is fascinating. It is a genetic anomaly-

137
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:07,280
an adaptation that is incredibly complex and yet is so ingenious that over the last 70 million

138
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:12,560
years it’s shown up completely independently all across the planet, from cacao in Peru

139
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:18,480
and Colombia, to the tea plant in the Himalayan foothills, Guarana in Brazil, the Kola Nut in West

140
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:24,320
Africa and of course, coffee in today’s Ethiopia. I’ll make this fast but basically caffeine is

141
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:30,960
an alkaloid compound; technically C8 H10 N4 02. It protects a plant from predators like

142
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:36,080
insects by causing a bitter flavor, and even acting as a toxin if consumed in high enough

143
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:40,880
doses. When coffee leaves and berries fall onto the forest floor they release caffeine

144
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:46,560
which poisons the topsoil, preventing any other plants from taking root, so all the nearby water,

145
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:51,520
nutrients and sunlight belongs only to them. And maybe the craziest effect is that in the

146
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:57,040
nectar of coffee flowers, there is exactly enough caffeine to get honeybees addicted,

147
00:14:57,040 --> 00:15:01,680
but not enough to cause them any harm. This means that in an entire biosphere,

148
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:08,080
bees that have tasted coffee will choose that plant to pollenate and ignore everything else.

149
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:12,640
Literally becoming hooked on caffeine. As far as we are concerned the way it

150
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:17,440
works is basically that during the day as we use energy our brain releases adenosine,

151
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:23,040
which builds up and makes us feel tired. We are calibrated to fill up our reserves of adenosine,

152
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:29,120
get drowsy and fall asleep. But caffeine blocks our adenosine receptors. It literally prevents us

153
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:34,640
from receiving the signal that we are exhausted. Obviously this does wear off, all of the adenosine

154
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:39,680
