166
00:16:49,520 --> 00:16:53,600
Around the end of the 14th century coffee arrived in Yemen, and we know it must have

167
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:58,800
caused a sensation, because all at once we see an explosion of writing from the Port of Aden,

168
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:04,640
describing a magical drink fueling Sufi prayers. At first this was referred to as Buna, the name

169
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:09,839
in Ethiopian. But soon enough it would given a new name, from old Arabic, translating to “the

170
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:16,400
Wine of Life.” This would be pronounced Qahwah. Beyond giving coffee its name, the Yemenites also

171
